<p id="mwAfk">Hermitage is located in the southern portion of Edmonton's northeast sector.<sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sectors_1-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sectors"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sectors-1" id="mwAfo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt215" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Plans_19-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Plans"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Plans-19" id="mwAf4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAf8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgA">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgE">]</span></span></a></sup> The area is bounded by 50 Street to the west, 130 Avenue and the Kennedale Ravine to the north, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Saskatchewan_River" title="North Saskatchewan River" id="mwAgI">North Saskatchewan River</a> valley to the east and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alberta_Highway_16" title="Alberta Highway 16" id="mwAgM">Yellowhead Trail</a> (Highway 16) and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_National" title="Canadian National" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAgQ">Canadian National</a> rail line to the south.<sup about="#mwt218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HGOP_23-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HGOP"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HGOP-23"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HGOP-23" id="mwAgU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgc">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgg">]</span></span></a></sup> The following three neighbourhoods comprise Hermitage.<sup about="#mwt219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wardsnbhds_5-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Ex